# Database
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# MySQL dumps and the PostgreSQL load script generated from them.
#
# These are excluded on purpose, not tidiness. Both hold real personal data:
# 781 accounts with scrypt password hashes, teacher names, and the text of
# disciplinary matters. They are the only copy of the pre-migration data, which
# makes them worth keeping — on the machine, and in a backup — and worth keeping
# out of git, which is not a backup.
#
#   database/tsc_case_management_dump.sql   the MySQL source, hand-exported
#   database/postgres-load.sql              generated by pnpm db:convert
#
# Named individually rather than as database/*.sql so that bootstrap.sql — which
# is source, and is what creates the local role — stays trackable.
#
# Regenerate the load script with `pnpm db:convert`; it is deterministic.
database/tsc_case_management_dump.sql
database/postgres-load.sql

# Any .env variant. DATABASE_URL carries the database password, so a stray copy
# under a different name is just as much of a leak as .env itself.
.env*
!.env.example

# Development-only object storage fallback (server/storage.ts). Holds uploaded
# files, so it must never be committed - it is not source and it is not a backup.
.local-storage/

# Generated by `pnpm db:sql` from drizzle/*.sql, for pasting into the Supabase
# SQL Editor. Not committed: it is a second copy of the schema, and a second
# copy is one that can drift from the migrations, which are the schema of record.
database/schema-apply.sql

# Webdev artifacts (checkpoint zips, migrations, etc.)
.webdev/
.project-config.json
.vercel

# Editor/agent worktrees. Untracked, but Tailwind reads .gitignore to decide what
# to scan - so an ignored-in-spirit directory that is not listed here still gets
# scanned, and a stale copy of the whole project ends up contributing class names
# to the shipped stylesheet. This one held 5 MB of an older checkout, including
# the login screen's previous colour scheme and components that no longer exist,
# and every class in it was being compiled into the CSS the officers load.
.kilo/

# The Figma Make scaffold the post-sign-in screen was designed in. Kept on disk
# as the design of record, and deliberately not committed: it is a complete
# second Vite + React + Tailwind project, with its own package.json and
# pnpm-lock.yaml, and a nested lockfile inside a pnpm repository is a trap for
# whatever tooling walks the tree looking for one. It also carries 2 MB of
# assets the repository already has elsewhere - the mark is at
# assets/brand/app-logo.png, and its crest.png is byte-identical to the emblem
# in assets/logos-img.
#
# What the design became is committed: client/src/components/BootLoader.tsx and
# the `boot-` rules in client/src/index.css. Regenerate this folder from Figma
# if the design needs revisiting; nothing in the application reads from it.
assets/Logo_Loader/
